WEBVTT

00:02.169 --> 00:03.636
Legend has it that...

00:04.805 --> 00:07.330
...during the Heian Period, there were
men who fought with no weapons.

00:07.941 --> 00:13.277
They were known as the Men of
Carnage and they reigned undefeated.

00:14.748 --> 00:19.913
Their technique was called
the Mutsu Enmei Style.

00:33.000 --> 00:40.429
<i>The Age of Chaos</i>
<i>Mutsu Enmei Style Gaiden</i>

00:40.707 --> 00:46.543
<i>Rushing through my innocent</i>
<i>youth without a care in the world.</i>

00:48.081 --> 00:53.986
<i>This soul of mine is</i>
<i>so easy to influence.</i>

00:55.656 --> 00:59.422
<i>WORRY ABOUT IDENTITY</i>

00:59.526 --> 01:02.723
<i>WORRY ABOUT IDENTITY</i>

01:06.500 --> 01:13.565
<i>This is what I'm wishing</i>
<i>for as I sing this song.</i>

01:13.740 --> 01:19.576
<i>I want you to acknowledge</i>
<i>me, that's all.</i>

01:20.447 --> 01:27.717
<i>You smiled at me for</i>
<i>the very first time.</i>

01:27.888 --> 01:36.296
<i>Thank you so much, thank you</i>
<i>from the bottom of my heart.</i>

01:36.997 --> 01:38.658
<i>I'll never forget it.</i>

01:48.442 --> 01:51.878
<i>Age of Chaos</i>
<i>Mutsu Enmei Style Gaiden</i>

01:54.748 --> 01:55.840
Who the hell are you?

01:58.252 --> 01:59.412
Bastard!

02:13.767 --> 02:14.825
I'm no liar.

02:15.936 --> 02:19.929
It wasn't the Shinsengumi
who killed him.

02:22.409 --> 02:23.774
I see...

02:24.344 --> 02:25.834
Sorry to bother you.

02:27.748 --> 02:31.707
You have attacked the
Shinsengumi headquarters.

02:31.852 --> 02:34.480
You're not going to slip away
without answering for that!

02:35.722 --> 02:38.418
I feel very lucky to have met you.

02:39.593 --> 02:43.723
I didn't perfect my skills all these
years just so I could kill others.

02:45.265 --> 02:48.792
I've reached the point where
I can believe that of myself.

02:51.171 --> 02:53.935
I want to challenge
you as just a swordsman...

02:54.074 --> 02:56.167
...not as a member of the Shinsengumi.

02:59.279 --> 03:01.975
It would give me no joy to
defeat you as you are now.

03:02.849 --> 03:04.544
Make a full recovery first.

03:06.286 --> 03:09.585
When you've recovered,
then I'll take you on.

03:09.890 --> 03:11.255
Is that a promise?

03:11.358 --> 03:13.826
When that day comes,
you'll really fight me?

03:15.095 --> 03:16.289
Yes.

03:22.970 --> 03:26.064
Lord Okita, you shouldn't
be walking in your condition.

03:26.673 --> 03:27.799
Don't worry.

03:27.941 --> 03:31.308
For some reason, my body
feels light as a feather today.

03:32.980 --> 03:34.277
Even so...

03:34.715 --> 03:38.947
Miss Ran, would you
please hand me my sword?

03:39.286 --> 03:40.275
What?

03:42.255 --> 03:43.517
Lord Okita?

03:43.624 --> 03:44.522
Thank you.

03:45.292 --> 03:46.987
This happens to kittens all the time.

03:49.830 --> 03:52.663
They can climb all the way
to the top of a tree, but...

04:02.676 --> 04:05.509
...then they find themselves
unable to climb down.

04:39.246 --> 04:41.714
You've lost weight, Okita.

04:43.917 --> 04:45.748
Have you recovered from your illness?

04:46.620 --> 04:49.555
Yes. I have recovered.

04:49.956 --> 04:51.184
Is that so?

04:55.662 --> 04:56.720
What?

04:58.765 --> 05:00.096
Who is he?

05:02.936 --> 05:09.500
<i>Like Snow</i>

05:11.878 --> 05:14.676
Not only did you manage to
avoid frightening the kitten...

05:14.815 --> 05:17.875
...you also sliced that
branch without disturbing him.

05:18.518 --> 05:20.816
Not even a master swordsman
could pull that off!

05:22.856 --> 05:25.290
Are you even more powerful now?

05:27.260 --> 05:28.522
Surely not!

05:30.964 --> 05:33.262
I think I might have become weaker.

05:35.268 --> 05:36.735
That can't be true.

05:40.040 --> 05:41.701
Every day...

05:42.809 --> 05:46.836
Every day, I thought about forsaking
my name as I looked at the sea.

05:48.148 --> 05:50.582
But then I remembered
I had a promise to keep.

05:51.485 --> 05:55.387
The person Lord Okita's
been waiting for, is it him?

05:56.389 --> 06:00.257
I never forgot about
that promise, not once.

06:01.728 --> 06:04.754
I really only came to
see how you were doing.

06:06.933 --> 06:09.060
I've lost some of my power...

06:09.169 --> 06:12.434
...and I was sure you'd be too
ill to even grasp your sword.

06:12.606 --> 06:13.903
That's what I thought on my way over.

06:15.842 --> 06:18.572
You say that you've lost
your power? It can't be true.

06:18.712 --> 06:20.179
You haven't changed at all.

06:21.381 --> 06:22.848
Six months ago...

06:24.818 --> 06:26.718
...that day you burst into the
Shinsengumi headquarters...

06:26.787 --> 06:28.345
...ready to attack...

06:29.089 --> 06:31.080
...you're the same
demon that you were then.

06:33.593 --> 06:35.322
Do I look that way to you?

06:35.962 --> 06:37.452
I cannot see you any other way.

06:39.399 --> 06:40.525
Is that right?

06:41.067 --> 06:43.865
If that's the case, then
it must be because of you.

06:44.905 --> 06:46.099
My blood...

06:46.473 --> 06:50.239
The Mutsu blood that's coursing
through my veins is coming to a boil.

06:52.445 --> 06:54.242
I'll ask you one more time.

06:54.347 --> 06:56.212
Have you made a full recovery?

06:59.319 --> 07:00.843
Yes, I have recovered.

07:01.621 --> 07:04.488
I want you to keep that promise now.

07:07.627 --> 07:09.094
I guess I will, then.

07:10.864 --> 07:12.354
You mean you were waiting...

07:12.699 --> 07:14.189
...to fight this man?

07:14.334 --> 07:15.801
Please don't!

07:22.442 --> 07:24.239
You're throwing away your scabbard?

07:24.778 --> 07:28.839
If I were Musashi, I'd say
that you'd already lost.

07:29.716 --> 07:31.809
You cracked my scabbard
before, you know...

07:35.288 --> 07:38.815
Anyway, I don't really
care about the outcome.

07:40.594 --> 07:44.257
All I want is to see
you go for the kill.

07:44.731 --> 07:46.323
Nothing more!

07:48.535 --> 07:51.333
Are you sure you're not
going to need that sword?

07:51.771 --> 07:54.239
The Mutsu Enmei Style
is to fight unarmed.

07:54.908 --> 07:55.966
Why don't I show you?

07:57.878 --> 08:00.813
But Lord Okita is far from well!

08:01.381 --> 08:03.281
Please, stop this madness!

08:16.630 --> 08:19.565
He has no intent to kill... and I
can't tell when he's going to strike.

08:20.567 --> 08:22.000
Not only that, but he's quick!

08:23.803 --> 08:25.930
Come on, I want you to bring it!

08:27.841 --> 08:30.674
All right, I still have
the strength to do this.

08:31.144 --> 08:32.736
Just let me hold on!

08:34.781 --> 08:36.442
Lord Okita...

08:40.453 --> 08:42.011
Why?

08:55.468 --> 08:56.366
What?

09:02.275 --> 09:04.539
W-Where did they...

09:19.726 --> 09:20.886
I've got him!

09:26.533 --> 09:28.433
A-Amazing!

09:29.803 --> 09:31.862
Right after you'd followed through with
your first kick...

09:32.072 --> 09:33.835
...who knew you'd strike again?

09:34.874 --> 09:36.671
Well, we're playing for keeps!

09:39.346 --> 09:42.907
Damn him, he even
dodged my Kogetsu kick!

09:47.153 --> 09:48.916
Unbelievable...

09:49.189 --> 09:50.622
...both of them!

09:57.564 --> 09:58.588
That first time...

09:59.466 --> 10:03.459
Do you remember the first time we met?

10:06.373 --> 10:07.567
Yes.

11:18.244 --> 11:19.575
Amazing!

11:20.880 --> 11:22.905
It's just like the first time we fought.

11:23.450 --> 11:24.974
You dodged my strike.

11:27.353 --> 11:29.048
It's not the same.

11:29.155 --> 11:31.885
Before it was a 2-step, this
time it was a 3-step thrust.

11:32.792 --> 11:36.125
It was all I could do to dodge that
thrust, so I couldn't get my kick in.

11:36.262 --> 11:39.356
Good, then maybe I didn't
have to throw away my scabbard.

11:56.282 --> 11:57.681
Lord Okita!

12:07.293 --> 12:08.385
Lord Okita...

12:09.329 --> 12:11.729
My strength is draining away.

12:11.831 --> 12:12.695
Not yet...

12:12.832 --> 12:15.198
I'm not done! Please, let me hold on!

12:18.338 --> 12:19.965
It's not over yet, is it?

12:20.640 --> 12:27.705
Don't call off the
fight just yet, please!

12:32.051 --> 12:37.353
I'm not ready to give up yet, Mutsu!

12:39.792 --> 12:43.091
Right. It's not over yet.

12:43.596 --> 12:46.258
Stop, please stop!

12:47.600 --> 12:49.795
Lord Okita is gravely ill!

12:49.936 --> 12:54.236
The truth is, he shouldn't even
be walking, that's how weak he is!

12:54.707 --> 12:57.039
And yet you still...

12:57.210 --> 12:58.370
Stay away!

13:04.784 --> 13:06.149
Lord Okita...

13:07.854 --> 13:10.482
Please, stay where you are.

13:11.257 --> 13:13.122
I want you to...

13:14.928 --> 13:19.058
...see me through this
until the very end.

13:22.135 --> 13:25.366
Now then, let's continue.

13:35.448 --> 13:36.745
It's so heavy...

13:36.849 --> 13:40.683
This sword seemed light as
a feather just moments ago...

13:42.155 --> 13:45.591
It's taking every ounce of strength
he has to hold that sword now...

13:45.725 --> 13:49.627
No, that's all the strength Lord
Okita has left in his condition!

14:02.208 --> 14:03.903
What a disgrace...

14:04.310 --> 14:10.112
...to think my own body would betray
me even at a crucial time like this!

14:12.986 --> 14:14.544
I'm a disgrace!

14:29.836 --> 14:31.667
On your feet, Okita!

14:33.773 --> 14:36.401
Get on your feet and show me
that thrust of yours again!

14:38.411 --> 14:41.141
I'm not even close to
going for the kill yet.

14:42.081 --> 14:46.745
I want to see Soushi Okita going
for the kill with that 3-step thrust!

14:49.188 --> 14:51.554
I swear I'll meet you head-on...

14:52.892 --> 14:54.792
Okita! Get up!

14:55.695 --> 14:57.458
On your feet, Okita!

15:13.513 --> 15:14.775
Snow...

15:14.914 --> 15:17.542
It can't be! It's early summer!

17:19.972 --> 17:22.167
That was an incredible thrust.

17:22.375 --> 17:26.334
Okita, you're a genius,
just like I thought.

17:28.581 --> 17:31.948
And your kick was nothing
short of miraculous.

17:41.227 --> 17:43.491
Lord Okita! No!

17:56.209 --> 17:57.938
Miss Ran...

17:59.679 --> 18:01.203
Thank you...

18:03.449 --> 18:07.647
Those words are all I
have to give you in return.

18:12.158 --> 18:13.386
Mutsu...

18:15.761 --> 18:18.127
I'm so glad I waited for you.

18:19.265 --> 18:21.665
You gave me the chance to take you
on...

18:22.134 --> 18:27.037
...and now I can die, not as
an invalid, but as a swordsman.

18:27.740 --> 18:30.834
I'm going to brag about
this to Kondo in heaven...

18:33.312 --> 18:36.873
There's just one last thing
I'd like you to do for me.

18:37.583 --> 18:38.914
Let's hear it.

18:40.219 --> 18:41.516
Go north...

18:41.888 --> 18:45.085
...and give this message
to Hijikata for me...

18:46.893 --> 18:50.090
"Soushi died a happy man."

18:51.130 --> 18:52.062
Mutsu...

18:54.233 --> 18:57.794
Take care of Hijikata for me, will you?

19:00.339 --> 19:01.931
All right.

19:04.744 --> 19:09.841
Lord Soushi!

19:12.218 --> 19:14.652
Snow, eh?

19:14.787 --> 19:17.756
Okita, it's a lot like you.

19:17.924 --> 19:22.020
So pure and cold and ephemeral...

19:23.763 --> 19:25.196
Murderer!

19:25.765 --> 19:27.892
Lord Okita was so ill...

19:28.200 --> 19:31.067
He couldn't even move,
and look what you did!

19:31.671 --> 19:32.865
Look what you did!

19:33.506 --> 19:34.700
Revenge!

19:47.753 --> 19:52.281
That was a good, clean strike,
suffused with your love for Okita.

19:55.094 --> 19:58.586
But it's not good enough to kill anyone.

20:00.666 --> 20:02.327
You murderer!

20:04.170 --> 20:07.469
That's right, I'm a murderer.

20:07.640 --> 20:09.801
I'm responsible for Okita's death.

20:11.844 --> 20:17.282
But he didn't lose to me,
he lost to his illness.

20:18.985 --> 20:24.252
I'd let you have your revenge, but
I have to keep my promise to Okita.

20:24.724 --> 20:28.387
Anyway, the first thing we
should do is lay him to rest.

20:33.633 --> 20:35.965
You're so light, Okita...

20:37.403 --> 20:40.236
I had no idea you were so light...

20:48.114 --> 20:56.146
<i>May 30, 1868, Soushi Okita was killed</i>
<i>in battle at Imado Hachihan, Edo...</i>

20:56.288 --> 21:01.453
<i>... at the age of 25.</i>

21:02.828 --> 21:08.994
There are no historical records
of a snowfall on this day.

21:10.670 --> 21:18.509
The legend of Soushi Okita, whose life
was like snow, is all that remains.

21:18.678 --> 21:20.475
<i>To be continued...</i>

21:31.624 --> 21:43.661
<i>Those summer stars, I looked up at</i>
<i>them alone when I was a troubled child.</i>

21:43.936 --> 21:53.675
<i>My loneliness and the vast night</i>
<i>sky, melting and shining in eternity.</i>

21:53.813 --> 22:02.812
<i>I just don't know what this</i>
<i>dream means, if it leads to love...</i>

22:02.955 --> 22:13.627
<i>Even if it's just "hello,"</i>
<i>I want to hear your voice.</i>

22:14.667 --> 22:20.799
<i>The person I am today</i>
<i>is about to disappear...</i>

22:21.173 --> 22:24.199
<i>What is it that will hold me back?</i>

22:25.044 --> 22:31.313
<i>Will it be you? I won't ask you now.</i>

22:31.617 --> 22:37.112
<i>Maybe if we ever meet again...</i>

22:51.871 --> 22:53.862
How long are you planning to follow
me?

22:54.006 --> 22:55.803
I'm not going to escape.

22:56.142 --> 22:58.303
I'm just going to see Hijikata.

22:59.645 --> 23:01.613
Next episode of the Age of Chaos...

23:01.781 --> 23:03.146
Going North.

23:03.249 --> 23:05.945
Pay close attention, and wait!
